  "text": {
    "intro": "The Dunnage Kite Festival charges by the kite, which has produced some creative definitions of 'one kite'.\nFive fliers are involved. Determine each flier's entry fee, kite and line.\n- **Flier**: Kipling, Tansy, Blaise, Morwenna and Gunnar.\n- **Entry fee** (listed from cheaper to dearer): $2, $4, $6, $8 and $10.\n- **Kite**: a rokkaku fighter, a box kite, a delta wing, a paper sled kite and a hand-painted dragon.\n- **Line**: nylon twine, braided dacron, hemp cord, kevlar thread and fishing monofilament.\nEvery flier has a different entry fee, kite and line, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The flier who uses braided dacron and $6 are exactly one fee step apart in entry fee order, in one direction or the other. The flier who flies a delta wing does not pay $6.",
      "Blaise and $10 are exactly one fee step apart in entry fee order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The flier who uses nylon twine pays $4.",
      "The flier who uses hemp cord is cheaper than the flier who flies a paper sled kite in entry fee order.",
      "The flier who flies a box kite is exactly one fee step cheaper than Tansy, with no entry fee in between.",
      "Tansy falls somewhere between the flier who uses fishing monofilament and the flier who uses kevlar thread in entry fee order, matching neither. Gunnar does not use kevlar thread.",
      "The flier who flies a rokkaku fighter is exactly one fee step cheaper than the flier who uses fishing monofilament, with no entry fee in between.",
      "Morwenna is exactly one fee step cheaper than the flier who flies a hand-painted dragon, with no entry fee in between."
